RUNIC BASTION — GATEWARD RUNE BARRICADE
Still source image for the first frame of an active-bastion animation

STATUS

This is a copy-ready prompt for one source still. It does not request
animation generation, asset import, or gameplay implementation.

REFERENCE IMAGE INPUT

Attach `assets_src/loadout/spell-cards/loadout_spell_runic_bastion_card.png`.
Use it as the visual source of truth for the dark gray stone blocks, warm
brass-gold reinforcement, luminous blue-cyan runes, and painterly fantasy
siege-game finish. Do not copy its fortress, gate architecture, landscape,
sky, trees, card framing, or full-scene composition. Create one isolated
barricade sprite.

PROMPT

Create exactly one still 2D fantasy-game battlefield sprite: the fully raised,
active Runic Bastion, a large fortified barrier positioned in front of an
allied gate. Compose it for a fixed side-view, orthographic 2D siege battlefield.
Show one contiguous, solid stone barricade with a broad readable front face,
a slightly crenellated top, two sturdy end-piers, and a central runic slab.
Its imposing silhouette should read as a physical obstruction that blocks
advancing ground units, not as an entire castle wall or fortress.

Build the barrier from chunky charcoal-gray stone blocks with restrained
warm-gold or brass edge bands and a few strong structural braces. Set one
large, unmistakable geometric rune into the central slab, with two or three
smaller matching marks on the end-piers. Illuminate the runes with clean
blue-cyan light matching the attached reference. Keep the energy contained to
the carved marks and their immediate seams; the masonry remains solid and
opaque enough to read as a destructible structure.

Show the barrier fully raised and intact, caught at a calm instant just after
activation. A few short, sharp cyan energy wisps may cling to the rune seams
to suggest that the magic has settled into the stone. Keep the overall shape
stable and legible at small battlefield scale. The bottom of the barricade
must sit on a consistent horizontal gameplay baseline near the lower part of
the canvas, with the complete top and both ends visible. Leave safe transparent
space around the silhouette.

Render only the Runic Bastion sprite. The fortress, gate, ground, terrain,
units, projectiles, and battlefield are absent; the game will composite the
sprite into the live battlefield. Keep the surrounding canvas genuinely
transparent. Do not add a dome, bubble, free-floating force field, floor,
landscape, or background glow that would obscure nearby gameplay. Use a
team-neutral blue-cyan rune glow; do not add faction emblems or text. No
health bar or HUD is part of the image.

For a later animation, the carved runes may pulse gently and a thin glint may
travel briefly along the seams, while the stone silhouette, scale, camera,
and bottom gameplay anchor remain fixed. This source still must show only one
instant, with no motion blur, impact, damage, cracks, collapse, or changing
construction state.

TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS

- Output exactly one PNG at 1024 x 576 pixels, landscape 16:9, RGBA with
  genuine alpha transparency.
- Use a transparent background, not a checkerboard, matte, or flat color.
- Keep the complete barricade and all glow at least 64 px inside every canvas
  edge. Do not crop a pier, rune, spark, or highlight.
- Keep the front face and rune geometry crisp and recognizable when scaled
  down to battlefield size.
- Keep the barrier centered horizontally and use a stable, level bottom
  baseline suitable for world-space compositing.
- Do not include animation, a sprite sheet, alternate takes, a contact sheet,
  labels, or variations.

